> f(x: u8) = (x >= 8) ? (1 << x) : x
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires 0 <= x < 8  (shift amount; C UB otherwise)
  defined at 8 of 256 points
  defined for: 0..7
  undefined e.g. at x=8; x=9; x=10; x=11
  C undefined behaviour at 248 points, e.g. x=8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap f
wrap analysis of f:
  1 << x   (u8)
      nuw holds
      nsw holds
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 0 points, e.g. 
      exact for: 0..7
  over all 256 points of the domain
